    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d897-a6">

                <pb facs="0873" n="775" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg775"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4.—Translations.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Newspaper clippings</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#center">[Che Kuk Sin Mun, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-04-14">April 14, 1900</date>.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>The foreign minister instructed the governor of Seoul to remove the electric
                    railway track along the pond outside the south gate to some other place, because
                    the station yard for the Seoul-Fusan Railway had been already discussed and
                    selected by the foreign minister, the minister for works, and the Japanese
                    minister.</p>
                <pb facs="0874" n="776" xml:id="pg776"/>
                <p rendition="#center">[Hwang Sung Sin Mun, April 14, 1900.]</p>
                <p>The Japanese minister wrote and asked for the removal of the electric railway
                    track outside the south gate to some other place, so that the Seoul-Chemulpo and
                    the Seoul electric railways would not mutually obstruct one another, and Ye Cha
                    Yun, the governor of Seoul, is going to have a consultation with the Japanese
                    minister and settle the matter.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
